From: Linux Fieldwork unit 19 <internal-packet>
Subject: [PATCH] tarfilter: regenerate shifted PAX ownership

Large numeric uid and gid values are carried by PAX extended headers. After
--idshift changes TarInfo.uid and TarInfo.gid, retained PAX uid/gid strings
still override the shifted fields when Python writes the output archive.

Drop only those stale numeric PAX keys after the validated shift. Python then
regenerates them from the shifted fields when the values require PAX encoding.
Other PAX metadata remains unchanged.

This patch is retained for internal preparation. External submission remains
unauthorized.
---
 tarfilter | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tarfilter b/tarfilter
--- a/tarfilter
+++ b/tarfilter
@@ -327,6 +327,8 @@ def main():
                     exit(1)
                 member.uid += args.idshift
                 member.gid += args.idshift
+                member.pax_headers.pop("uid", None)
+                member.pax_headers.pop("gid", None)
             if hasattr(args, "trans"):
                 for r, s in args.trans:
                     member.name = r.sub(s, member.name)
